            "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/cython/cython/commits/af9a8415c3e4182dd0b180fc2ff5e28a8361f5a4/comments",
            "commit": {
                "author": {
                    "date": "2026-08-23T06:40:08Z",
                    "email": "andrew.teylu@vector.com",
                    "name": "Andrew V. Teylu"
                },
                "comment_count": 0,
                "committer": {
                    "date": "2026-08-23T07:43:57Z",
                    "email": "andrew.teylu@vector.com",
                    "name": "Andrew V. Teylu"
                },
                "message": "Avoid MSVC C4551 on unused-helper \"touch\" statements\n\nCython marks conditionally-unused static helper functions as \"used\" to\nsilence -Wunused-function by referencing them in a discarded expression.\nSeveral sites did this with a bare function name, e.g.\n\n    (void)__Pyx_PyObject_CallMethod0;\n\nMSVC reads a bare function name as a call that is missing its argument\nlist and emits warning C4551. Take the function's address instead:\n\n    (void)&__Pyx_PyObject_CallMethod0;\n\nThis is unambiguous (it cannot be parsed as a call), is valid C and C++\non every compiler, still marks the symbol as used, and matches the\n(void)&func idiom already used elsewhere in CythonFunction.c.\n\nConverted every bare-function \"touch\" site: ExtensionTypes.c (the\n__Pyx_PyType_Ready helper pulled in by every extension type),\nMatchCase.c, ObjectHandling.c, Optimize.c, TString.c, ModuleSetupCode.c,\nFunctionArguments.c, StringTools.c, and the __Pyx_TraceReturnCValue\nmacro in Profile.c (whose convert_function argument is always a bare\nto_py_function name). Genuine unused-variable touches such as (void)ptr;\nare left untouched, since C4551 only applies to functions.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code (Opus 4.8), pair-programming with the author\nSigned-off-by: Andrew V. Teylu <andrew.teylu@vector.com>",
                "tree": {
                    "sha": "608d70b8fc96a13757d3d699c2e249b39a0111b1",
